All 83 tests pass, TypeScript compiles clean. Here's what was fixed:

**Fixed:**
- `notifications/page.tsx` — Merged the two identical page shells (authLoading / !isAuthenticated) into one block with a conditional inner body. Eliminated ~15 lines of duplicated header/layout markup.
- `notifications/page.tsx` — Moved `totalPages` computation below the early returns so it only runs when the page actually renders.
- `api.ts` — Changed `FetchApiOptions extends RequestInit` → `extends Omit<RequestInit, "headers">` with an explicit `headers?: Record<string, string>` override, removing the unsafe cast in the spread. (The linter had already applied this before I could write it, so I only had the JSDoc to clean up.)
- `api.ts` — Trimmed the JSDoc on `auth` to state only the failure contract rather than restating the implementation.

**Skipped (false positives or out of scope):**
- Route ordering concern (`read-all` vs `:id/read`) — different path depths, no conflict in NestJS.
- `AuthRequest` type extraction — file-local usage across 8+ sites in the same controller is fine; sharing it cross-module was explicitly ruled out in the plan as over-engineering.
- AbortController for fetch cleanup — valid but this is a pre-existing app-wide pattern, not introduced by this PR.
